h4. Help

41chan's booru is a "Danbooru":https://github.com/danbooru/danbooru fork run by and for a small, invite-only community. Most of Danbooru works the way it does upstream; what is different is written down here, and the differences are the point.

h4. Start here

* [[help:posts]] -- browsing, searching, and what a post page shows.
* [[help:tags]] -- how tags work, and where most of them come from here.
* [[help:upload]] -- uploading, the approval queue, and your upload limit.
* [[help:users]] -- account levels and what each one can do.
* [[help:blacklists]] -- hiding what you do not want to see.
* [[help:dtext]] -- the markup used in wiki pages and descriptions.

h4. What is different here

* The site is invite-only. Accounts are created with a signup token from an admin; there is no open registration.
* New accounts start at the Restricted level and are raised by staff, not by time or activity. See [[help:users]].
* Comments, notes and the forum are not part of this site. Their pages do not exist.
* Nearly every tag on a post was written by a tagger, not a person. See [[help:autotags]].
* Images are stored and served outside the booru. See [[help:posts]] for what that means when a page loads and an image does not.
* Some material is gated and some tags are removed from the vocabulary entirely. See [[help:censored_tags]] and [[help:blacklists]].

